  "content": "Frontend has no @/lib/types.ts — deleted. All API response shapes are defined as zod schemas in @/lib/schemas.ts, and the TS types are inferred via `z.infer\u003ctypeof XSchema\u003e` and exported alongside. api.ts parses every response through the matching schema so wire-format drift between Go and React throws a ZodError at the boundary instead of silently corrupting downstream rendering. Component prop types stay INLINE above each component (`type FooProps = {...}` then `function Foo({...}: FooProps)`), never in a shared barrel. Helpers: `listOf(itemSchema)` builds the {items: [...]} envelope, `request(schema, path)` and `requestList(listSchema, path)` are the two fetch paths. zod 4.x.\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003ctags\u003e[\"frontend\", \"typescript\", \"validation\", \"convention\"]\u003c/tags\u003e",
